# Bulk Failure Summary Test

This test documents the fail-soft batch semantics: when one issue in a
multi-ID batch fails, the other issues are still applied (each with its own
jj commit as usual), every failed ID is reported with the operation, the ID,
and the reason, the IDs that were NOT applied are listed, and the command
finishes with an `N/M succeeded` summary and a non-zero exit code. On the
happy path the output remains one compact line per changed issue with no
summary noise. Single-issue batches print exactly what the per-issue command
prints.

## Setup: a dependency edge (Login required_for Second)

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles link 11111111 required_for 22222222
✓ Added relationship

```

## A batch whose second source would close a dependency cycle

Third -> Login applies; Second -> Login would close the
Login -> Second -> Login cycle and fails per-issue. The applied source keeps
its compact line; the failure summary names the failed ID with its reason,
lists what was NOT applied, and finishes with the N/M succeeded count.

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles link 33333333 22222222 required_for 11111111
? failed
✓ Added relationship: 333 required_for 111
Link failed for 222: Cannot add relationship Second bug required_for Login bug: it would create a dependency cycle
Not applied: 222
1/2 succeeded

```
